IMPORT prelude

-- Annotated Code of Maryland, Human Services Article, Title 5, Subtitle 3: the Family Investment Program (FIP) and its
-- temporary cash assistance (TCA), Maryland's TANF programme. Who may be eligible (s 5-308(a)(2), (3), (h)); the conditions
-- for receiving TCA (s 5-312(b)); exemptions from, and good cause for, the work activity requirement (s 5-308(b), (c)); good
-- cause for not cooperating with child support (s 5-308(d)); the most work activity that may be required (s 5-308(a)(6),
-- (7)); education as work activity (s 5-308(a)(4)); the time limits (s 5-313); SSI left out (s 5-315(b)); the sanctions,
-- the 30-day conciliation period and the bar on reducing assistance within 30 days of the first notice (s 5-312(e)); and
-- transitional assistance (s 5-312(f)).
--
-- SEAT: the parent, caretaker relative or pregnant individual who applies for, or receives, temporary cash assistance:
-- "Can my family get TCA? Must I do work activity, and for how many hours? Can my grant be cut, by how much and when?"
-- Provisions addressed to the Department, the Secretary or a local department are encoded for what they mean to that
-- person.
--
-- Edition: the Code as in effect on 1 October 2026 (mgaleg.maryland.gov, 'include enactments of the last session'), as
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/human-services-title-5-subtitle-3-family-investment-program.txt.
--
-- The amount of TCA is set by the Secretary's regulations (COMAR Title 07), which are not deposited (the COMAR host refused
-- the commons fetcher; see the Maryland README). The grant amount and the part of it designated for the adults are inputs.
-- "All other FIP requirements that the Secretary establishes by regulation" (s 5-308(a)(3)(iv)) is asked as a fact.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the Department's planning, hiring, contracting and reporting duties (ss 5-303 to 5-307, 5-316 to 5-323);
-- welfare avoidance grants beyond their cap (s 5-309(a)(2)); the substance abuse screening (s 5-314); sponsor deeming for
-- legal immigrants (s 5-312(d), a federal rule; asked as part of the income test, which is not encoded); s 5-310 (both
-- contingency versions); the hardship exemption standards of s 5-313(b) (asked as a fact).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Family Investment Program -- temporary cash assistance`

§§ `s 5-308(a)(2), (3), (h); s 5-312(b); s 5-313 -- can my family get temporary cash assistance`

-- s 5-308(a)(2): "A family may be eligible for assistance under this subtitle only if the family includes: (i) a minor child
-- who resides with a custodial parent or other adult caretaker who is a relative of the child; or (ii) a pregnant
-- individual."
GIVEN `my family includes a minor child living with a custodial parent or an adult caretaker relative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my family includes a pregnant individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the family may be eligible under s 5-308(a)(2)` IF
        `my family includes a minor child living with a custodial parent or an adult caretaker relative`
    OR  `my family includes a pregnant individual`

-- s 5-308(b): the Secretary's exemption criteria "shall include exemptions for: (i) ... adults who are required to care for
-- a child who is a recipient under the age of 1 year"; "(ii) ... adults and children who are recipients and who are severely
-- disabled", limited by (4) to 12 months "unless: (i) the individual applies for Supplemental Security Income; and (ii) the
-- application is approved, pending, or on appeal"; "(iii) adults who have not received assistance for at least 6 months".
GIVEN `I care for a recipient child under 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am severely disabled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `months I have been exempt for severe disability` IS A NUMBER
      `I have applied for SSI and the application is approved, pending or on appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have not received assistance for at least 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am exempt from the work activity requirement under s 5-308(b)` IF
        `I care for a recipient child under 1`
    OR  (    `I am severely disabled`
         AND (   `months I have been exempt for severe disability` LESS THAN 12
              OR `I have applied for SSI and the application is approved, pending or on appeal`))
    OR  `I have not received assistance for at least 6 months`

-- s 5-308(a)(3): "Assistance shall be provided to an applicant or recipient under this subtitle only if the applicant or
-- recipient: (i) resides in the State at the time of application for assistance; (ii) if applicable: 1. has applied for child
-- support services ...; and 2. complies with the requirements of the local child support enforcement office; (iii)
-- participates in work activity under this subtitle; and (iv) meets all other FIP requirements that the Secretary establishes
-- by regulation." Read with (b)(1) (an exempt individual "may not be required to meet the work activity requirement"), (d)(2)
-- (no denial for "good cause for noncooperation with child support") and (e)(1) (nor for an "adequate reason").
-- s 5-312(b)(2): TCA only if the applicant "assigns to the State all right, title, and interest in support"; (b)(3): a minor
-- parent must live with a parent or adult relative payee, in an adult-supervised group home, or independently where a
-- social worker confirms safety requires it (asked as one fact).
-- s 5-313(a): no TCA to a family with an adult who "(1) has received more than 60 cumulative months" of federally funded TCA,
-- or "(2) ... more than 24 cumulative months ... and (ii) is not participating in a work activity"; from (1) only, a local
-- department may exempt the family for hardship under (b)(1) (asked as a fact).
DECLARE `Can my family get TCA` IS ONE OF
    `yes: my family meets the conditions of ss 5-308(a) and 5-312(b), so it is entitled to temporary cash assistance (s 5-312(c)), at the amount the regulations set`
    `no: the family must include a minor child living with a custodial parent or adult caretaker relative, or a pregnant individual (s 5-308(a)(2))`
    `no: I must reside in Maryland when I apply (s 5-308(a)(3)(i))`
    `no: I must apply for child support services and comply with the child support office, unless I have good cause or an adequate reason (s 5-308(a)(3)(ii), (d), (e))`
    `no: I must take part in work activity, unless I am exempt (s 5-308(a)(3)(iii), (b))`
    `no: I must meet the other FIP requirements set by regulation (s 5-308(a)(3)(iv))`
    `no: I must assign my rights to child support to the State while we receive TCA (s 5-312(b)(2))`
    `no: as a minor parent I must live with an adult relative payee, in an adult-supervised group home, or independently where a social worker confirms it is needed (s 5-312(b)(3))`
    `no: an adult in my family has received more than 60 months of federally funded TCA and the family has no hardship exemption (s 5-313(a)(1))`
    `no: an adult in my family has received more than 24 months of federally funded TCA and is not participating in a work activity (s 5-313(a)(2))`
    `no: a legal immigrant who arrived on or after 22 August 1996 and is eligible for federally funded cash assistance is not entitled under s 5-308(h)`

DECLARE `My FIP application` HAS
    `minor child with a custodial parent or caretaker relative` IS A BOOLEAN
    `pregnant member`                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `resides in Maryland at application`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `child support services applied for and complied with`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `good cause or adequate reason for child support`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `participates in work activity`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `exempt from work activity`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `meets the other regulatory requirements`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `assigns support rights to the State`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `a minor parent`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `minor parent's living arrangement is one s 5-312(b)(3) allows` IS A BOOLEAN
    `most months of federally funded TCA received by an adult`  IS A NUMBER
    `hardship exemption from the 60-month limit`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `a legal immigrant who arrived on or after 22 August 1996`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `eligible for federally funded cash assistance`             IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `a` IS A `My FIP application`
GIVETH A `Can my family get TCA`
`the TCA decision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the family may be eligible under s 5-308(a)(2)` (`a`'s `minor child with a custodial parent or caretaker relative`) (`a`'s `pregnant member`)))
            THEN `no: the family must include a minor child living with a custodial parent or adult caretaker relative, or a pregnant individual (s 5-308(a)(2))`
        IF (NOT (`a`'s `resides in Maryland at application`))
            THEN `no: I must reside in Maryland when I apply (s 5-308(a)(3)(i))`
        IF (NOT (`a`'s `child support services applied for and complied with` OR `a`'s `good cause or adequate reason for child support`))
            THEN `no: I must apply for child support services and comply with the child support office, unless I have good cause or an adequate reason (s 5-308(a)(3)(ii), (d), (e))`
        IF (NOT (`a`'s `participates in work activity` OR `a`'s `exempt from work activity`))
            THEN `no: I must take part in work activity, unless I am exempt (s 5-308(a)(3)(iii), (b))`
        IF (NOT (`a`'s `meets the other regulatory requirements`))
            THEN `no: I must meet the other FIP requirements set by regulation (s 5-308(a)(3)(iv))`
        IF (NOT (`a`'s `assigns support rights to the State`))
            THEN `no: I must assign my rights to child support to the State while we receive TCA (s 5-312(b)(2))`
        IF `a`'s `a minor parent` AND (NOT (`a`'s `minor parent's living arrangement is one s 5-312(b)(3) allows`))
            THEN `no: as a minor parent I must live with an adult relative payee, in an adult-supervised group home, or independently where a social worker confirms it is needed (s 5-312(b)(3))`
        IF `a`'s `most months of federally funded TCA received by an adult` GREATER THAN 60 AND (NOT (`a`'s `hardship exemption from the 60-month limit`))
            THEN `no: an adult in my family has received more than 60 months of federally funded TCA and the family has no hardship exemption (s 5-313(a)(1))`
        IF `a`'s `most months of federally funded TCA received by an adult` GREATER THAN 24 AND (NOT (`a`'s `participates in work activity`))
            THEN `no: an adult in my family has received more than 24 months of federally funded TCA and is not participating in a work activity (s 5-313(a)(2))`
        IF `a`'s `a legal immigrant who arrived on or after 22 August 1996` AND `a`'s `eligible for federally funded cash assistance`
            THEN `no: a legal immigrant who arrived on or after 22 August 1996 and is eligible for federally funded cash assistance is not entitled under s 5-308(h)`
        OTHERWISE `yes: my family meets the conditions of ss 5-308(a) and 5-312(b), so it is entitled to temporary cash assistance (s 5-312(c)), at the amount the regulations set`

§§ `Questions for the applicant -- eligibility`

@export Can my family get Maryland temporary cash assistance (TCA) under the Family Investment Program?
GIVEN `minor child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your family includes a child under 18 who lives with you as their custodial parent, or with another adult relative who cares for them
      `pregnant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone in your family is pregnant
      `live in Maryland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you live in Maryland now, when you apply
      `child support cooperation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have applied for child support services with the local child support office and are doing what it asks (answer TRUE if there is no other parent to seek support from)
      `child support good cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have good cause or an adequate reason not to cooperate with child support (for example a risk of harm to you or the child, rape or incest, a pending adoption, a family crisis)
      `doing work activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are taking part in work activity (job search, work, training, community service, or education related to employment)
      `care for baby` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you must care for a child under 1 who is part of your TCA case
      `severely disabled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are severely disabled
      `months exempt for disability` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months you have already been exempt from work activity because of severe disability (0 if never)
      `SSI application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have applied for Supplemental Security Income and the application is approved, pending or on appeal
      `no assistance for 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have not received assistance for at least the last 6 months
      `other requirements met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you meet the other FIP requirements set by the Department's regulations (for example income and resource limits)
      `assign support` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you agree to assign to the State your family's right to child support for the time you receive TCA
      `minor parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a parent under 18
      `minor parent arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Minor parents only: whether you live with a parent, guardian or adult relative who will be your payee, in an adult-supervised group home, or on your own where a social worker confirms your or your child's safety needs it
      `months of TCA` IS A NUMBER @desc The most months of federally funded TCA (or TANF) any adult in your family has received in total
      `hardship exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the local department has exempted your family from the time limit because of hardship
      `immigrant after 1996` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a legal immigrant who arrived in the United States on or after 22 August 1996
      `eligible for federal cash assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Immigrants after 1996 only: whether you are eligible for federally funded cash assistance
GIVETH A `Can my family get TCA`
`Can my family get temporary cash assistance` MEANS
    `the TCA decision` (`My FIP application` WITH
        `minor child with a custodial parent or caretaker relative` IS `minor child`
        `pregnant member`                                           IS `pregnant`
        `resides in Maryland at application`                        IS `live in Maryland`
        `child support services applied for and complied with`      IS `child support cooperation`
        `good cause or adequate reason for child support`            IS `child support good cause`
        `participates in work activity`                             IS `doing work activity`
        `exempt from work activity`                                 IS `I am exempt from the work activity requirement under s 5-308(b)` `care for baby` `severely disabled` `months exempt for disability` `SSI application` `no assistance for 6 months`
        `meets the other regulatory requirements`                   IS `other requirements met`
        `assigns support rights to the State`                       IS `assign support`
        `a minor parent`                                            IS `minor parent`
        `minor parent's living arrangement is one s 5-312(b)(3) allows` IS `minor parent arrangement`
        `most months of federally funded TCA received by an adult`  IS `months of TCA`
        `hardship exemption from the 60-month limit`                IS `hardship exemption`
        `a legal immigrant who arrived on or after 22 August 1996`  IS `immigrant after 1996`
        `eligible for federally funded cash assistance`             IS `eligible for federal cash assistance`)

@export Am I exempt from the FIP work activity requirement (s 5-308(b))?
GIVEN `care for baby` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you must care for a child under 1 who is part of your TCA case
      `severely disabled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are severely disabled
      `months exempt for disability` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months you have already been exempt because of severe disability (0 if never)
      `SSI application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have applied for Supplemental Security Income and the application is approved, pending or on appeal
      `no assistance for 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have not received assistance for at least the last 6 months
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I exempt from work activity` IF
    `I am exempt from the work activity requirement under s 5-308(b)` `care for baby` `severely disabled` `months exempt for disability` `SSI application` `no assistance for 6 months`

§§ `s 5-308(a)(4), (6), (7) -- how much work activity may be required of me`

-- s 5-308(a)(6): "The Department may require a work-eligible individual to participate in work activity for a maximum of:
-- (i) 30 hours per week for an individual with a child at least 6 years old; (ii) 20 hours per week for a single parent or
-- caretaker relative with a child under the age of 6 years; (iii) a combined average of 35 hours per week for a family with
-- two work-eligible parents who do not receive federally funded child care assistance; or (iv) a combined average of 55 hours
-- per week for a family with two work-eligible parents who receive federally funded child care assistance", the last
-- "provided that an adult in the family does not have a disability or is not caring for a child with a disability"
-- (NOTES.md finding 3). (7): the individual may choose to do more, "up to a maximum of 40 hours per week".
DECLARE `My household for work activity` IS ONE OF
    `a single parent or caretaker relative with a child under 6`
    `an individual whose youngest child is at least 6`
    `two work-eligible parents without federally funded child care`
    `two work-eligible parents with federally funded child care`

DECLARE `How many hours may be required` IS ONE OF
    `hours`         HAS `per week` IS A NUMBER
    `not stated, because an adult in the family has a disability or cares for a child with a disability, so (iv) does not apply (s 5-308(a)(6)(iv))`

GIVEN `text` IS A STRING
GIVETH A `My household for work activity`
`the household named` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `text` EQUALS "single parent with a child under 6"   THEN `a single parent or caretaker relative with a child under 6`
        IF `text` EQUALS "two parents without child care"       THEN `two work-eligible parents without federally funded child care`
        IF `text` EQUALS "two parents with child care"          THEN `two work-eligible parents with federally funded child care`
        OTHERWISE `an individual whose youngest child is at least 6`

GIVEN `household` IS A `My household for work activity`
      `an adult in the family has a disability or cares for a child with a disability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `How many hours may be required`
`the most work activity the Department may require` MEANS
    CONSIDER `household`
    WHEN `a single parent or caretaker relative with a child under 6` THEN `hours` 20
    WHEN `an individual whose youngest child is at least 6` THEN `hours` 30
    WHEN `two work-eligible parents without federally funded child care` THEN `hours` 35
    WHEN `two work-eligible parents with federally funded child care` THEN
        IF `an adult in the family has a disability or cares for a child with a disability`
        THEN `not stated, because an adult in the family has a disability or cares for a child with a disability, so (iv) does not apply (s 5-308(a)(6)(iv))`
        ELSE `hours` 55

@export What is the most work activity, in hours a week, the Department may require of me (or of us, combined) under s 5-308(a)(6)?
GIVEN `household` IS A STRING @desc Your household. One of: "single parent with a child under 6", "parent with a child at least 6", "two parents without child care", "two parents with child care" (two work-eligible parents, with or without federally funded child care assistance)
      `disability in the family` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an adult in your family has a disability or cares for a child with a disability
GIVETH A `How many hours may be required`
`How many hours of work activity may be required of me` MEANS
    `the most work activity the Department may require` (`the household named` `household`) `disability in the family`

-- s 5-308(a)(4): the Department "shall allow" the work activity requirement to be met "for a maximum of 24 months" by "(i) a
-- minimum of 20 hours per week of vocational education that leads to an associate degree, a diploma, or a certificate; or
-- (ii) an average of at least 20 hours per week of education directly related to employment". (5): the Department may
-- suspend this for new applicants when the work participation rate is low (asked as a fact).
@export Does my education count as my FIP work activity (s 5-308(a)(4))?
GIVEN `hours of education a week` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours a week (on average, for education related to employment) you spend in vocational education leading to an associate degree, diploma or certificate, or in education directly related to employment (adult basic education, English as a second language, GED)
      `months already counted` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months education has already counted as your work activity
      `suspended for new applicants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a new applicant and the Department has suspended this rule for new applicants under s 5-308(a)(5)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my education count as work activity` IF
        `hours of education a week` AT LEAST 20
    AND `months already counted` LESS THAN 24
    AND (NOT `suspended for new applicants`)

§§ `s 5-312(e) -- can my grant be cut, and by how much (only if I have been found not to comply)`

-- s 5-312(e)(1)(i): "a 30% reduction of the portion of a recipient's grant amount designated for the adult member or
-- members, minor parent or parents, or pregnant individual" for noncompliance "without good cause, with FIP work activity
-- requirements"; (ii): the children's portion "may not be reduced or terminated" for it. (2): "a 25% reduction of the entire
-- grant amount" for noncompliance "without adequate reason or good cause with child support requirements". Both are taken
-- of the unreduced amounts (NOTES.md finding 2). (5): "the full amount ... shall resume on compliance". s 5-308(b)(5): an
-- exempt individual who volunteers for work activity is not reduced for it; s 5-308(a)(7)(ii): no reduction for working fewer
-- than 40 hours while meeting the minimum requirement.
GIVEN `grant amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the part designated for the adults` IS A NUMBER
      `found in noncompliance with work activity without good cause` IS A BOOLEAN
      `found in noncompliance with child support without good cause or adequate reason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have since complied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the grant after the s 5-312(e) reductions` MEANS
    IF `I have since complied`
    THEN `grant amount`
    ELSE `grant amount` MINUS `the work reduction` MINUS `the child support reduction`
    WHERE
        `the work reduction` MEANS
            IF `found in noncompliance with work activity without good cause`
            THEN 30% TIMES `the part designated for the adults`
            ELSE 0
        `the child support reduction` MEANS
            IF `found in noncompliance with child support without good cause or adequate reason`
            THEN 25% TIMES `grant amount`
            ELSE 0

@export How much temporary cash assistance will I get after a sanction for not complying with work activity or child support requirements (s 5-312(e))?
GIVEN `grant amount` IS A NUMBER @desc Your family's monthly TCA grant before any reduction, in US dollars (set by the Department's regulations)
      `adult portion` IS A NUMBER @desc The part of that grant designated for the adults, minor parents or pregnant individual in your case, in US dollars
      `work noncompliance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an adult or minor parent in your case has been found not to comply with work activity requirements, without good cause, after the 30-day conciliation period
      `child support noncompliance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an adult or minor parent in your case has been found not to comply with child support requirements, without good cause or adequate reason, after the 30-day conciliation period
      `now complying` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have since complied with the requirement
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much TCA will I get after a sanction` MEANS
    `the grant after the s 5-312(e) reductions` `grant amount` `adult portion` `work noncompliance` `child support noncompliance` `now complying`

-- s 5-312(e)(3)(i): "If a recipient is found to be in noncompliance with FIP requirements, the local department shall
-- provide a 30-day conciliation period for each instance of noncompliance"; (4): "The Secretary may not reduce or terminate
-- temporary cash assistance to a family until 30 days after the day on which the first written notice of noncompliance was
-- sent to the recipient." As regulative rules, counted in days from the day the first written notice was sent (day 0).
DECLARE `FIP party` IS ONE OF `the recipient`, `the Department`
DECLARE `FIP act` IS ONE OF
    `comply with the FIP requirement`
    `reduce or terminate the family's temporary cash assistance`

GIVETH A DEONTIC `FIP party` `FIP act`
`s 5-312(e)(4) -- no reduction or termination until 30 days after the first written notice` MEANS
    PARTY  `the Department`
    SHANT  `reduce or terminate the family's temporary cash assistance`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the Department` BECAUSE "temporary cash assistance reduced or terminated within 30 days after the first written notice of noncompliance (s 5-312(e)(4))"

-- The recipient's side: complying within the conciliation period keeps the full grant; if not, the Department may then
-- reduce it (s 5-312(e)(1)-(3)); and if the recipient complies afterwards, the full amount resumes (e)(5).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `FIP party` `FIP act`
`s 5-312(e)(3) -- I may comply within the 30-day conciliation period, failing which my assistance may be reduced` MEANS
    PARTY  `the recipient`
    MUST   `comply with the FIP requirement`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST
        PARTY `the Department`
        MAY   `reduce or terminate the family's temporary cash assistance`

@export How many days after the first written notice of noncompliance must pass before my temporary cash assistance can be reduced or terminated (s 5-312(e)(4))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How long before my TCA can be cut` MEANS 30

§§ `s 5-312(f) -- transitional assistance (only after TCA has been terminated)`

-- s 5-312(f)(1): "After termination of temporary cash assistance under this section, a recipient may receive transitional
-- assistance." (2): if the caseworker determines it is appropriate, the FIP benefit "shall be paid instead to a third party
-- payee on behalf of the recipient for a period of up to 3 months". (8): the recipient "may reapply for the FIP benefit".
@export After my TCA was terminated for noncompliance, for how many months at most can my benefit be paid to a third party for me as transitional assistance (s 5-312(f)(2))?
GIVEN `the caseworker finds it appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your caseworker has determined that transitional assistance is appropriate for you
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many months of transitional assistance` MEANS
    IF `the caseworker finds it appropriate` THEN 3 ELSE 0

§§ `s 5-315(b) -- SSI is not counted`

-- s 5-315(b): "In determining a family's eligibility for the FIP, the local department shall exclude Supplemental Security
-- Income (SSI) benefits provided to an adult or child family member."
@export How much of my family's income counts for FIP eligibility, once SSI is left out (s 5-315(b))?
GIVEN `family income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your family's total monthly income, in US dollars
      `SSI in it` IS A NUMBER @desc The Supplemental Security Income included in that total, for any adult or child in the family, in US dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much income counts for FIP eligibility` MEANS `family income` MINUS `SSI in it`
